# kfind configuration template
# kfind is a file finding utility (similar to KDE's KFind), not a network service.
# It does not listen on ports, does not connect to databases, and has no runtime dependencies
# on other services in the capability vocabulary.
#
# Configuration is typically handled via command-line arguments or desktop environment
# settings (KDE/Qt), not via a standalone configuration file in /etc.
# This template exists to satisfy structural requirements but produces no functional
# network or service directives.

# No configuration directives required for kfind.
# If custom search scopes or filters are needed, they are passed via CLI:
# kfind <path> --filter <filter_expr>
# See 'man kfind' for available options.